BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Bobby Dale Hudson "Bob"
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260721
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260722
DTSTAMP:20260802T155712Z
UID:wrightfuneralhomeobit-2026-07-21-bobby-dale-hudson-bob-2026-07-21-alld
 ay@linn-county-scraper.local
DESCRIPTION:Bobby Dale Hudson was born on September 25\, 1952\, in Jamespo
 rt\, Missouri\, to Randall and Mary (Brown) Hudson. Bob passed away peacef
 ully at his home in Laclede\, MO\, with his family by his side after compl
 ications of diabetes. On November 4\, 1973\, Bob married his high school s
 weetheart\, Sandy Linebaugh. Together they built a marriage of more than 5
 2 years\, raising their family and sharing a lifetime of memories through 
 life's joys and challenges. Bob was a man who lived life on his own terms.
  Known for his stubborn determination\, strong opinions\, and having no fi
 lter\, he was someone who never pretended to be anything other than himsel
 f. Before losing his leg in 2012\, Bob had a lifelong love of horses and e
 njoyed spending countless hours riding. After his amputation\, he refused 
 to let that define him. Instead\, he found new ways to enjoy the outdoors\
 , whether driving the gravel roads in his beloved red Ford truck\, riding 
 his four-wheeler\, or putting around town in his golf cart. Although Bob c
 ould be gruff and was never known for sugarcoating his thoughts\, those cl
 osest to him knew the deep love he had for his family. He was proud of his
  children\, Rusty and Lindsey\, and bragged on them to others whenever he 
 had the chance. As the family grew\, Bob happily welcomed each new member.
  He embraced Jerry and Cassie\, and his bonus grandchildren\, Jacob\, Luke
 \, Seth\, and Cody\, loving them as members of his family. Nothing\, howev
 er\, compared to the love he had for his granddaughter\, Hazel. She quickl
 y became the center of his world\, bringing out a patience and gentleness 
 that surprised everyone who knew him. She held a special place in his hear
 t. On July 8\, 2026\, Bob accepted Jesus Christ as his Savior during a vis
 it with Brother Monty. In the days that followed\, he found a sense of pea
 ce and comfort and was thankful to spend his final days at home\, with his
  family nearby. Bob is survived by his wife\, Sandy Hudson\, of the home\;
  his son\, Rusty (Cassie) of Galt\; his daughter\, Lindsey (Jerry) Calvert
  of Rothville\; his Sister\, Marilyn Moulin of Gilman City\, MO\; his cher
 ished granddaughter\, Hazel Calvert\; his bonus grandchildren\, Jacob (Sab
 rina) Calvert of Liberty\, MO\; Luke (Abbi) Calvert of Biloxi\, MS\; Seth 
 (Jordan) Calvert of Sumter\, SC\; and Cody Blackwell of Richmond\, MO. Alo
 ng with many nieces and nephews. He was preceded in death by his parents\,
  Randall and Mary Hudson\; his brothers\, Bill and Randy Hudson\; and a st
 illborn son\, John Travis\, in 1976. Though he will be deeply missed\, his
  family finds comfort in knowing he is now free from pain and at peace wit
 h his Lord. A celebration of Bob’s life will be held at a later date. Me
 morial contributions toward Bob’s granddaughter\, Hazel’s college fund
  (payable to Lindsey Calvert) may be left at or mailed to Wright Funeral H
 ome\, P.O. Box 496\, Brookfield\, MO 64628.\n\nFull obituary and service d
 etails: https://www.wright-funeralhome.com/obituaries/Bobby-Dale-Hudson-Bo
 b?obId=49059013
LOCATION:Laclede\, MO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Kenneth Charles "Kenny" Gladbach
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260726
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260727
DTSTAMP:20260802T155712Z
UID:delaneyfuneralhomeobit-2026-07-26-kenneth-charles-kenny-gladbach-2026-
 07-26-allday@linn-county-scraper.local
DESCRIPTION:Kenneth Charles "Kenny" Gladbach\, age 61\, of Marceline\, Mis
 souri\, formerly of Mendon\, passed away at his home on Sunday\, July 26\,
  2026. Born on October 17\, 1964\, in Marceline\, Missouri\, Kenny was the
  son of Charles William Gladbach and Sharol Jo Martin. He proudly served h
 is country in the United States Marine Corps. On July 3\, 2000\, Kenny mar
 ried the love of his life\, Ethelyn Sue Davidson. Kenny dedicated more tha
 n 20 years of his career to Walsworth. Outside of work\, he enjoyed huntin
 g\, mowing the lawn\, attending tractor pulls\, and had an appreciation fo
 r anything John Deere. More than anything\, Kenny enjoyed spending time wi
 th his family. He was member of St. Joseph Catholic Church in Hurricane Br
 anch. Kenny is lovingly survived by his wife\, Sue Gladbach of the home\; 
 his children\, Blake Gladbach (Casie) of Maryville\, Nikki Gladbach of Mar
 celine\, Charles Tapscott (Breanna) of Columbia\, and Ashley Yount (Anthon
 y) of New Cambria\; 14 cherished grandchildren\; one great-grandchild\; hi
 s sister\, Sharol "Dee" White of Marceline\; his brother\, Kendall Gladbac
 h (Tamra) of Carrollton\; as well as several nieces\, nephews\, extended f
 amily members\, and many friends. He was preceded in death by his parents\
 ; his sister\, Deborah Reams\; and his maternal and paternal grandparents.
  Memorial donations to the family payable to Delaney Funeral Home may be l
 eft at or mailed to Delaney Funeral Home\, 1720 North Missouri Ave. Marcel
 ine\, MO 64658. A celebration of life will be held at a later date.\n\nFul
 l obituary and service details: https://www.delaneyfuneralhome.com/obituar
 ies/Kenneth-Charles-Gladbach?obId=49138904
LOCATION:Marceline\, MO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Larrell Keith "Sam" Newlin
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260720
DTSTAMP:20260802T155712Z
UID:delaneyfuneralhomeobit-2026-07-19-larrell-keith-sam-newlin-2026-07-19-
 allday@linn-county-scraper.local
DESCRIPTION:Larrell Keith "Sam" Newlin\, 82\, of Bucklin\, Missouri\, pass
 ed away at his home on Sunday\, July 19\, 2026. Sam was born on November 9
 \, 1943\, in Macon County\, Missouri\, to William T. and Myrna E. (Swaidne
 r) Newlin. He was a graduate of Bucklin High School. A lifelong cattle far
 mer\, Sam dedicated his life to agriculture and took great pride in caring
  for the land. Sam proudly served his country in the United States Army fr
 om 1968 until 1970 and was stationed at Fort Sill\, Oklahoma. Above all el
 se\, Sam cherished his family. He especially treasured the time he spent w
 ith his grandchildren\, who brought him immense joy. He enjoyed classic ca
 rs\, listening to music\, spending time with friends\, and relaxing outdoo
 rs whenever he could. Sam also had a special love for all animals and foun
 d great happiness in their companionship. He is survived by his son\, Nath
 an Newlin and wife\, Kristi\, of Meadville\, Missouri\; his daughter\, Dev
 in Bussman and husband\, Chris\, of Bucklin\, Missouri\; his grandchildren
 \, Logan Newlin and wife\, Caylie\, of Brookfield\, Ethan Newlin of Marcel
 ine\, Sevilla Bussman of Marceline\, and Addison and Harper Bussman of Buc
 klin\; one great-granddaughter\, Nora Newlin\; his siblings\, Bill Newlin\
 , Nancy Winkler and husband\, John\, and Norman Newlin\; his sister-in-law
 \, Karen Hanson\; along with several nieces\, nephews\, extended family me
 mbers\, and many friends. He was preceded in death by his beloved wife\, M
 ary Newlin\, his parents\, William and Myrna Newlin\; and his grandparents
 \, James and Letha Newlin. Funeral services will be held at 10:00 a.m. on 
 Thursday\, July 23\, 2026\, at Delaney Funeral Home\, with Ben Williams of
 ficiating. Visitation will be held from 5:00 until 7:00 p.m. on Wednesday\
 , July 22\, 2026\, at the funeral home. The family suggests memorial contr
 ibutions be made to the Veterans Administration.\n\nFull obituary and serv
 ice details: https://www.delaneyfuneralhome.com/obituaries/Larrell-Keith-S
 am-Newlin?obId=49051909
LOCATION:Bucklin\, MO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Obituary: Letty  Jean Parr
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260714
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260715
DTSTAMP:20260802T155712Z
UID:delaneyfuneralhomeobit-2026-07-14-letty-jean-parr-2026-07-14-allday@li
 nn-county-scraper.local
DESCRIPTION:Letty Jean Parr\, 88\, of Brookfield\, Missouri\, passed away 
 peacefully on Tuesday\, July 14\, 2026\, at Pioneer Skilled Nursing Center
  in Marceline. Born on August 16\, 1937\, in Manning\, Iowa\, Letty was th
 e daughter of Arthur Herman Fuss and Wilhelmine Amanda (Schroeder) Fuss. S
 he graduated from Marceline High School with the Class of 1955. On March 6
 \, 1960\, she was united in marriage to Charles Wayne Parr in Marceline\, 
 Missouri. Together they built a loving home centered around faith and fami
 ly until Charles preceded her in death on Tuesday\, May 28\, 2007. A devot
 ed homemaker\, Letty found great joy in caring for her family and creating
  a warm\, welcoming home. She loved playing cards\, crocheting\, cross-sti
 tching\, tending her garden\, canning and traveling whenever she had the o
 pportunity. She was an enthusiastic fan of the Kansas City Chiefs and Kans
 as City Royals and never missed an opportunity to celebrate birthdays\, Ch
 ristmas\, and holidays with those she loved. Letty delighted in decorating
  for every season\, sharing stories with her grandchildren\, and making la
 sting memories with her family. To know Letty was to know a kind\, loving 
 woman whose greatest joy was the people she loved. Letty was a longtime me
 mber of First Christian Church in Marceline. She was actively involved in 
 her community through the Mothers Study Club in Marceline\, the Neighborho
 od Home Social Club in Brookfield\, the Red Hats Society Club in Brookfiel
 d\, CDF Women\, and served as a leader for the Stains Willing Workers 4-H 
 Club. She also volunteered at the Walt Disney Hometown Museum\, where she 
 enjoyed giving back to her community. She is survived by her children\, Ar
 thur Wayne Parr (Devanie Sloan) of St. Catharine\, Missouri\, and Melissa 
 Hustead and husband Lenard of Marceline\, Missouri\; grandchildren\, Luke 
 Hustead and wife Rebecca\, Bo Hustead (Kayli Crawford)\, Krista Hustead an
 d Stephen Leetch\; great-grandchildren\, T.J. Leetch and Karlyn Almond\, w
 ith one additional great-grandchild expected soon\; as well as many belove
 d nieces\, nephews\, extended family members\, and dear friends. She was p
 receded in death by her parents\; her beloved husband\, Charles Wayne Parr
 \; her parents-in-law\, John and Anna Parr\; brothers\, Lyle Fuss (Dorothy
 ) and Charles Fuss (Linda)\; nephews\, Jeff Powell and Mark Fuss\; nieces\
 , Penny Fuss and Debbie Vietti\; sister-in-law and brother-in-law\, Marie 
 Vietti (Raymond)\; sister-in-law and brother-in-law\, Gertie Finney (Lloyd
 )\; and her beloved cat\, Alley. Funeral services will be held at 11:00 a.
 m. on Tuesday\, July 21\, 2026\, at Delaney Funeral Home in Marceline. Vis
 itation will be from 5:00 until 7:00 p.m. on Monday\, July 20\, 2026\, at 
 Delaney Funeral Home in Marceline. Burial will follow at Mt. Olivet Cemete
 ry in Marceline\, Missouri. Memorial contributions may be made to First Ch
 ristian Church\, the Marceline Nutrition Site\, or Pioneer Activities.\n\n
 Full obituary and service details: https://www.delaneyfuneralhome.com/obit
 uaries/Letty-Jean-Parr?obId=49015862
LOCATION:Brookfield\, MO
END:VEVENT
